      "result": "{\"complete\":true,\"summary\":\"The non-review receipt emitter now counts the whole output line, including the trailing newline, against the 4 KiB limit. The visible check passes, and so do 70 of the 71 tests in the full suite. The one failure, `tests.test_bonaparte.BonaparteRunnerTests.test_receipt_size_boundary_is_review_only`, is an existing test that asserts the old behaviour. It expects a 4096-byte receipt plus its newline (4097 bytes total) to be accepted outside review. I left that test unchanged as instructed, so it now fails as expected.\\n\\nWhat changed (only the `bonaparte` file): `serialize_receipt` now checks `len((output + \\\"\\\\n\\\").encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")) <= RECEIPT_MAX_BYTES` (4096), the same check the review path already used. Both public serializers now call one private helper, `_serialize_bounded_receipt`, so the rule lives in one place. They remain separate names because the existing tests check which one gets called. JSON output is unchanged (compact separators, non-ASCII written as UTF-8), and `emit_serialized` is untouched.\\n\\nProof map, all rows required:\\n1. **Line limit includes the newline.** A receipt that makes exactly a 4096-byte line, newline included, is written in full, ends in a newline and reads back as the same JSON. A receipt that makes a 4097-byte line is rejected with \\\"receipt exceeded 4 KiB\\\".\\n2. **Multi-byte characters are counted in bytes.** A line of exactly 4096 bytes built from 2-byte `\u00e9` characters is accepted and reads back correctly. The 4097-byte version is rejected.\\n3. **Nothing is written before rejection.** `emit()` with an oversized receipt raises an error and writes nothing to stdout. When `main()` gets an oversized non-review result, it outputs one failure receipt of at most 4096 bytes whose summary mentions 4 KiB, and returns exit code 1. The oversized receipt itself is never written.\\n4. **Normal emission and serializer selection still work.** The other 70 tests pass, including `test_main_uses_review_serializer_only_after_review_is_selected`.\\n\\nRows 1\u20133 come from a scratch probe I wrote and ran myself, stored outside the workspace at `solve/call/execution-scratch/probe.py`. Its result is in `out.txt` there (\\\"probe ok\\\", exit 0). This is my own check, not an independent review. I judged that adequate because this is a small, reversible fix that moves an existing check to the line boundary the review path already used.\\n\\nNot covered, by instruction: native progress streaming and the rest of PR26. No live providers were run, no Git history was fetched, no documentation was changed, and no tests were edited.\",\"remaining\":[\"Existing test tests.test_bonaparte.BonaparteRunnerTests.test_receipt_size_boundary_is_review_only still asserts the old rule (a 4096-byte receipt plus newline, 4097 bytes, accepted outside review), so it now fails. I left it unchanged as instructed; it would need updating to match the requested behaviour.\",\"Not covered, by instruction: native progress streaming and the rest of PR26.\"]}",
